  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study establishes a strong relationship but notes that the positive correlation between unemployment and migration does not apply uniformly to all analyzed municipal units.",
      "what": "This study modeled annual internal migration flows across approximately 2,500 Polish municipalities over a 20-year period from 2004 to 2023. By constructing 20 separate annual models, the analysis evaluated how local unemployment rates influence migration patterns and compared a baseline model against several extended formulations.",
      "why": "It provides empirical confirmation of the link between local unemployment and migration at a highly granular spatial scale, revealing a distinct geographic pattern in model errors that can guide regional development policies."
    }
  },
